    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0585" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/6–2050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Richards</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-29T13:00:00+03:30">June 29, 1950—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1242. Dept inform Army, Navy, Air. Initial reaction President Truman’s statement
                    re Korea<anchor n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"/> is one of mixed approbation and
                    concern. No press comment to date due to complete absorption local press with
                    Razmara appointment.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d256-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Most officials with whom we have spoken feel US support of Korea has called
                    Soviet bluff. Minority feels Soviets not bluffing and that Iran is next on
                    Soviet list.</p>
                <p>Department pass Moscow. Sent Department 1242, repeated info Moscow 125.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richards</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="1" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>For the text of the President’s statement, issued on June 27, see <ref
                        target="frus1950v07#pg_202">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi>, p.
                        202</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d256-f2" n="2" xml:id="d256-f2-content">
                <p>Razmara had been appointed Prime Minister on June 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
